NAH. Honestly it sounds like your neice has/had some real issues. Those issues could have arisen from being abused. I would like you to consider that for a moment - your 11 year old neice was quite possibly being abused. Say that to yourself. Put your neice in the position of being the victim rather than your bf. 

&amp;#x200B;

I'm not saying your bf did anything (although I hope you considered at least that it is possible) and her behaviour may have been acting out seeking help. That help doesn't appear to have come.

INFO with a most likely NTA: Do you not really 'do' birthdays in your family? I know there are religions out there that tend to put a dampner on celebrations. Also how old are you?

&amp;#x200B;

Honestly though, the fact you are responding to this by learning not to get your hopes up makes me really sad. Treat others as you want to be treated - I guess they are all showing you how they want to be treated.

Thanks for the support - all I wanted to point out was that OP is risking his entire relationship with his daughter here and he may want to rethink that. I went against the prevailing view though, so this is my punishment.

I hope I'm wrong, but I get the impression that OP is more controlling than he lets on in this post

&amp;#x200B;

I know this is a bit late and totally no longer relevant per your edit, but NTA for preparing vegan food. You ask a vegan to cook - you will get vegan food. Its not rocket science. I don't think there is any selfishness there at all.

&amp;#x200B;

You would be TA though if you use this as a way to "convert" the guests - nobody likes a preachy vegan.

This is a difficult one. I am ex-big 4 myself so I understand what he is going through (no MBA though - that seems needlessly tough). The work life balance thing *can* get better when you leave the big 4 but its by no means guaranteed. The highest paid jobs still require a large amount of overtime although there are plenty of decently paid ones that have a more standard set of hours. I'm assuming he is about to qualify as an accountant which comes with a nice pay rise. Would be still be earning less once he qualifies? The long term earning potential of both your careers needs to be factored in somewhere.

&amp;#x200B;

That said, I'm going NTA becuase even if he is working hard, you shouldn't be left feeling like a single parent doing 98% of the household stuff and he doesn't seem open to solutions. Also, WTF "who cares if you don’t get promoted" thats a shitty thing to say. The "lost touch with life long best friends because he wasn’t comfortable with me having male friends" is also a worry as that makes him come accross as pretty insecure and controlling.

&amp;#x200B;

One question though - why are you using a babysitter that doesn't meet your needs? Can't you find one that is better suited to your hours?

&amp;#x200B;

The resentment is an issue - if you want to fix your marriage then you both need to work on that (him on resolving the things that cause resentment and you on letting go of it). If you don't want to save the marriage then there isn't much to do. You can't judge people on how you think the future will be, only on what they show you now.

&amp;#x200B;

Good luck

This makes him TA. Anyone with mental health issues that affect other people that aren't trying to fix them suck. You should stop enabling him - it won't help him in the long run.

&amp;#x200B;

The small rural town has no cafe/bar etc?

This isn't the legal advice sub, but if I were your friend I would counter sue you for storage costs. Location will matter hugely - but it would cost you min $50 per month to store a car in an unheated garagem so $1,200 for 2 years. You may end up losing money as well as a friend here.

&amp;#x200B;

Also - your comment about "only" one death is a pretty asshole thing to say. That turned this into a hard YTA from me. Maybe ESH because I'm not sure of the legality of her driving your car, but mosty YTA for that comment.

NTA - your relationship does not sound healthy. Sorry to say. Witholding or withdrawal of love and affection is a serious act of emotional abuse, as is tell you that she is the only person who cares for you (isolating you further). Getting cold feet about moving in is also not a betrayal and to portray it that way is not healthy.

&amp;#x200B;

I know you think you love her, but I don't think she is good for you

Probably a bit late, but pick where you want your elevators first. The three options senible options are:

* Elevator room room room elevator
* Room elevator room elevator room
* room elevator elevator room room

&amp;#x200B;

Clear out one section of your vault enough to get an elevator going all the way down, then you can build rooms at the bottom to store your dwellers whilst you clear out the rest and build the other elevators. 

&amp;#x200B;

In terms of good layouts, there are too many. Personally I like production rooms at the top (power rooms in the centre), training and crafting rooms in the middle and then living a storage rooms (plus the office and theme room if thats your thing) at the bottom. 

&amp;#x200B;

For the unpopulated rooms at the bottom you probably want to build in some fire breaks as otherwise events will take forever to complete.
